  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "NAR database updates (RNAactDrug 2.0, LncRNAfunc 2.0, R-loopBase v2.0, iGPSC-DB) land alongside new fusion, chimeric RNA and methylation-based cancer tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure for interpreting cancer omics, mainly curated resources and detection tools. Database releases expand reference layers. RNAactDrug 2.0 links RNA, CNV, mutation, methylation and enhancer features to drug sensitivity. LncRNAfunc 2.0 integrates TCGA, GTEx, CCLE, binding and perturbation evidence for cancer lncRNAs. R-loopBase v2.0 reanalyses 358 datasets from 16 technologies with quantitative confidence scoring, and iGPSC-DB catalogs inferred single-cell genetic perturbations. A second strand addresses transcript-structure discovery. RIFTT combines Arriba and FusionCatcher with new scoring metrics to cut fusion false positives. A separate integrative pipeline yields 569,640 chimeric RNAs across 1019 cancer cell lines and uses dependency screening to link candidates to fitness. DNA methylation underpins two tools. MANTIS predicts time-dependent survival and treatment effects in childhood brain tumors from 2,786 patients. XenoMix quantifies mouse content in PDX methylation arrays. CALM, an AML single-cell and bulk atlas, and TailEnrich, a tail-enrichment test for subset-specific dysregulated genes, complete the set.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
